codex
The root cause is now concrete: this runner exposes mismatched PID and `/proc` namespaces—`getpid()` returns an inner PID, while `/proc/<pid>/exe` is mounted for outer PIDs. Lean 4.22 resolves its executable via exactly that path, so it fails before reading the project. I’m applying a narrowly scoped preload shim in `/tmp/audit-work` that makes `getpid()` return the numeric `/proc/self` target, then rerunning the unchanged trusted preflight.
apply patch
